{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "laplace_beltrami_interior",
    "description": "Interior-only metric spherical Laplacian (Laplace-Beltrami) on the latlon grid: the doubly-interior 5-point cross value lap u = (1/(R_sphere^2 cos^2 phi)) d2u/dlambda^2 + (1/(R_sphere^2 cos phi)) d/dphi(cos phi du/dphi) over i in [2,NLON-1], j in [2,NLAT-1] (lambda=lon, phi=lat in RADIANS; dlambda=(pi/180)dlon_deg, dphi=(pi/180)dlat_deg, pi=3.141592653589793). ZONAL term: the centered per-radian second difference (u[i+1,j]-2u[i,j]+u[i-1,j])/(R_sphere^2 cos^2 phi_j dlambda^2) -- the per-degree D2 of central_D2_lon_interior scaled by the (180/pi)^2/(R_sphere^2 cos^2 phi_j) metric weight (the cos(lat) weighting that distinguishes this from the bare per-degree operator). MERIDIONAL term: the conservative (mimetic) flux-form divergence of the cos-weighted gradient, (cos(phi_{j+1/2})(u[i,j+1]-u[i,j]) - cos(phi_{j-1/2})(u[i,j]-u[i,j-1])) /(R_sphere^2 cos phi_j dphi^2), with the cell-face latitudes phi_{j+-1/2} at the half-index nodes -- the standard 2nd-order finite-volume Laplace-Beltrami stencil that annihilates constants and is discretely conservative in the meridional flux. cos(phi) at cell centers and faces is computed IN THIS BODY from phi_j=(pi/180)(lat0_deg+(j-1)dlat_deg) and phi_{j+-1/2}=(pi/180)(lat0_deg+(j-1+-1/2)dlat_deg): free-name geometry (lat0_deg, dlat_deg, dlon_deg, R_sphere) resolves in the consuming model's scope at evaluation (the grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/latlon/grid.esm). VALID ONLY on a REGIONAL spherical patch with lat strictly inside (-90,90) so cos phi>0 everywhere (a spherical cap/band); the global pole-cap treatment of the 1/cos^2 zonal singularity at phi=+-90 is a documented FOLLOW-UP. Match-less named template consumed by the boundary-condition rule layer (rules/laplace_beltrami_lon_periodic_lat_zero_grad). O(dlon_deg^2)+O(dlat_deg^2) on this uniform index space.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:latlon",
      "op:laplacian",
      "order:2",
      "stencil_width:5"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Williamson, D. L., Drake, J. B., Hack, J. J., Jakob, R., & Swarztrauber, P. N. (1992). A standard test set for numerical approximations to the shallow water equations in spherical geometry. Journal of Computational Physics, 102(1), 211-224. (Laplace-Beltrami / covariant Laplacian on the sphere.)"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Chapter 2 (finite-volume flux-form divergence of a variable-coefficient gradient) and the [1,-2,1] second difference."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "laplace_beltrami_interior": {
      "params": [
        "u"
      ],
